ols e5 and d4), **P: d2-d4** (claims center), or **P: d2-d3** (solid but slower).\n\nReason:  \n**N: g1-f3** is excellent because it develops a knight to its most active square, supports central pawns, doesn’t block the d-pawn, and prepares castling. It’s a cornerstone of many openings. While d2-d4 is also good, playing the knight first keeps flexibility in the center.\n\nAnswer: N: g1-f3"}
