ent, and creates immediate tactical tension.\n\nReason:  \nPushing the d-pawn to d6 increases pressure on Black’s position, limits counterplay, and potentially opens the e-file or diagonal for White’s pieces. It also prevents Black from comfortably developing or castling. The pawn on d6 will be hard to dislodge and may require immediate attention from Black, giving White the initiative.\n\nAnswer: P: d5-d6"}
